  AnalyzerLines:
  - 'A cracked stone tablet: ''DAY 412. STILL DIGGING. THE DEPOT SAYS THE BONUS IS
    COMING.'''
  - A precursor coin stamped with a pickaxe crossed over a star. Their currency was,
    apparently, also ore.
  - A mural fragment showing tiny figures carrying glowing stones toward a tower
    of light.
  - An ancient helmet lamp, still faintly warm. Whoever wore it was digging in the
    same direction you are.
  - A rusted automaton gear, inscribed with a serial number older than any known
    civilization.
  - 'A carved warning in an unknown script. The Analyzer''s best guess: ''Below the
    fire, the silence. Below the silence, the Makers.'''
  - 'A curator''s tag sealed in resin: ''Exhibit 1 of many. Return to Museum.'' Someone
    expected you.'
  - A child's toy shaped like a little drill. Some things never change.
  - A map etched into bone, showing the layers as rings around a sleeping heart at
    the center of the world.
